seg-048b6c3a9f0c = Numbers in human text use the language's decimal mark (a comma in { "15" } of the { "18" } languages; a point in en, ja, zh-Hans and en-XA). Numbers in machine files always use the point. A count (a variable named <c1/>, <c2/>, <c3/>, <c4/> or <c5/>) reaches Fluent as a number, so a translation may write <c6/>.

